{"results":[{"url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/archive/updated-inventory-lists-in-historical-exhibits","final_url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/archive/updated-inventory-lists-in-historical-exhibits","title":"Newly Updated Inventory Lists in Historical Exhibits","description":null,"language":"en","text":"# Newly Updated Inventory Lists in Online Exhibits\n\nThe World Bank Group Archives regularly publishes online exhibits on interesting topics in the institution’s history. In some cases, inventory lists containing archival records relevant to the topic are included. These lists can help researchers who want to dig deeper into our history by accessing archival records. In cases where the material has been declassified and digitized, links to these records are also provided in the inventory lists. Recently, the Archives updated the lists in the following exhibits to reflect the latest information about disclosure status and to include links to newly digitized records.\n\n---\n\n* A Bold Vision to Defeat River Blindness\n\n  The World Bank Group’s first foray into the health sector was one of its most successful.\n* In 1958, India was threatened by a balance of payments crisis midway through its Second Five-Year Development Plan. The Indian government requested the World Bank Group to organize additional financial support.\n* The World Bank's Role as Mediator in the 1950s\n\n  A small number of prominent Bank-led mediation efforts in the 1950s illustrate how the World Bank extended itself beyond loans to facilitate economic development.\n* Bretton Woods and the Birth of the World Bank\n\n  On July 1, 1944, delegates from 44 nations met at the secluded Mount Washington Hotel in Bretton Woods, New Hampshire to participate in what became known as the Bretton Woods Conference.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n---\n\nCheck out other exhibits authored by the World Bank Group Archives. These exhibits, which range in topic from historic firsts to impactful personalities and whimsical reflections, help illuminate the rich history of the institution. In each exhibit, you will find archival records and photographs selected from our holdings.\n\n---","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":240.93449899919506,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}